meta {
  name: Manually retry the failed task (API equivalent of Cockpit "Increment retries")
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

put {
  url: {{engineRest}}/external-task/{{failedTaskId}}/retries
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "retries": 3
  }
}

docs {
  # Manual retry

  This re-arms the failed order external task with fresh retries — exactly what the Cockpit
  "Increment retries" button does. Because BIKE-FAIL is a *permanent* simulated outage, the task
  will run, fail again, and the incident returns once the retries are exhausted. That is the
  teaching point: a manual retry re-runs the work but is not a fix for a systematic error. To
  demonstrate an actual fix, start a fresh request with a valid bike id (e.g. BIKE-900) and watch
  it complete.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}
